From 380fe3ae1f5199717536c84298988c1b3f09e5c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ubadream <noreply@ubadream.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:51:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Carry the bound request across continue compactions

A bound continue compaction removes the request it covered, so a later
prepare with no new user message could not bind. Carry the request the
binding recorded over this thread's continue notice, treat a handoff
already delivered as stale, and remove the covered request by identity
instead of popping the last message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
